in the aftermath of elon musk winning  approval from twitter's board to buy the  company for 44 billion dollars  tesla shareholders showed their doubts  shares of the electric car maker fell  nearly 12 on april 26th  erasing nearly 130 billion dollars from  tesla's market cap  this took out 29 billion dollars from  musk's fortune in less than a day  this happened because most of musk's  fortune lies in his 21 stake in tesla  when musk first proposed a hostile  takeover of twitter on april 14th  analysts pointed out concerns musk could  be forced to pledge tesla shares as  collateral for loans to buy the social  media company some of those fears have  come to fruition as part of the 46.5  billion dollar financing package musk  revealed on april 25th he will pledge  62.5 billion dollars worth of tesla  stock to secure a 12.5 billion dollar  margin loan  and prior to going after twitter  musk had already pledged more than half  his stake in tesla as collateral for  other loans  on top of a 13 billion debt commitment  from banks which will partly be secured  by twitter itself musk also told  twitter's board he will pay for 21  billion dollars of the purchase with  equity however it's not yet clear where  that cash will come from forbes  estimates musk has about 2 billion  dollars of cash on hand after selling  over 16 billion dollars worth of tesla  shares late last year  paying taxes on those sales donating six  billion dollars to a charitable entity  and paying 2.6 billion dollars to  acquire his initial twitter stake  earlier this year
 

